#### 5. Eager Test
**Test:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)
```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```
**Risk:** 7 distinct production methods called. When this test fails, you must debug which of the 7 calls broke. It's unclear what behavior is actually under test.
**Fix:** If this is intentionally an integration/workflow test, mark it explicitly with `[TestCategory("Integration")]`. Otherwise, split into focused unit tests for each method and test the workflow via an integration test:
```csharp
[TestCategory("Integration")]
[TestMethod]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

