## Smell-Free Pattern ✨

**`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException`** (line 155) is well-written:
- Uses `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` instead of try/catch
- Asserts on a specific property (`ex.ParamName`)
- Single clear behavior under test
- No magic numbers, no external dependencies

This is the pattern to follow for exception tests.

